        "kind": "text",
        "text": "Base rate/reference class: for one-month-ahead forecasts of this exact ONS CPI annual-rate series, the strongest base rate is persistence plus recent monthly changes. The latest three headline CPI annual rates were 3.3%, 2.8%, and 2.8%, averaging 2.97% if using March-May but 2.87% if downweighting March's pre-April energy-price-cap step. Since the June 2025 base month already had a 0.3% monthly CPI rise, June 2026 needs a monthly rise materially above 0.3% to push the annual rate above 2.9%."
